# a11y capture: yt-shorts-then-home-tab
# device: Pixel 3 (192.168.1.68:5555), Android 12 / API 31. Captured 2026-09-12.
# HOW: tools/qa/reblock-on-tab-tap-probe.sh with DWELL=150 -- YouTube force-stopped, cold-launched
#      (it opens on Shorts), its 3-second DELAY overlay left to auto-complete, swiped on Shorts for
#      150 seconds, then the in-app Home tab tapped, then the feed used.
# EXPECTED (test oracle): the caption on the Home feed must be the GENERIC items label. Detection
#      reports SHORTS while the pager is up and null once the feed is, so a caption detected on
#      Shorts is not valid on the feed.
# WHAT IT PROVES (issue #28 FAIL 1 + FAIL 2, device QA 2026-09-12):
#      1. YouTube's Shorts pager emits ZERO TYPE_VIEW_SCROLLED across 150 seconds of swiping. The
#         single scroll event in this capture is the home feed's `com.google.android.youtube:id/results`
#         list, and the single click is the tab tap itself. This is the already-filed Shorts limitation, and it is why the reported run showed
#         "no counter activity at all on Shorts" -- not a regression.
#      2. The caption bug, live: at 00:34:33.973 detection reported feature=null, at 00:34:33.989 an
#         interaction was counted, and at 00:34:34.015 the overlay was shown `label=shorts` over the
#         home feed. The invalidation added for this could never fire, because
#         `detectAndEvaluateFeature` did `detectFeature(...) ?: return` and so never told the handler
#         about a null.
#      3. What it does NOT show: a second block. One `handling block` line for YouTube across the
#         whole run, no picture-in-picture at any point, and no sitting end -- even past the
#         two-minute return window. The reported second overlay needed a service REBIND, which
#         sequence B of tools/qa/issue28-device-verify.sh forces deliberately.
